## ═══════════════════════════════════════
## SEO keyword tiers (Physiq strategy)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════

Classify keywords **by search intent and competition**, then place them deliberately. Macro Academy guides are **not** the place to brute-force homepage “money” terms in every paragraph.

### Tier 1 — Core money keywords (homepage & calculator)

- **Role:** Highest volume / highest competition; protect the homepage, `/#calculator`, and primary product surfaces.
- **Typical use in Academy:** **Sparingly**—primary Tier‑1 term in `metaTitle` / `title` **only** when the article truly matches that query; **one** natural mention in intro or closing CTA; otherwise link with descriptive anchor to **`/#calculator`** or the relevant **`/macros/...`** hub instead of repeating the phrase.
- **Examples — “from search” (illustrative high-demand head terms):** macro calculator, free macro calculator, TDEE calculator, calorie calculator, calorie and macro calculator, macro calculator online, best free macro calculator.
- **Examples — “recommended” / brand-aligned (support positioning, still competitive):** Physiq macro calculator, macro calculator app, macro tracking app, free macro calculator no signup, macro and calorie calculator for weight loss.
- **Do not** treat either list as copy-paste boilerplate for every guide.

### Tier 2 — Goal-based keywords (audience & phase)

- **Role:** **Primary mapping for most Macro Academy articles**—fat loss, muscle gain, women/men, keto, high protein, cutting, recomp, PSMF calculator, maintenance, bulking, etc.
- **Use:** Natural **H2/H3** targets where the section answers that intent; 1–2 in-body mentions where it reads human; align **`relatedMacroSlugs`** (and in-body links) with these intents—e.g. `cutting-macros`, `high-protein-macro-calculator`, `keto-macros`, `maintenance-macros`—**verify slugs exist** under `lib/seo/pages` or published guides before shipping.

### Tier 3 — Long-tail / question keywords (high intent)

- **Role:** Specific questions and “how to / what should I” queries; strong for snippets and depth.
- **Use:** **Subheadings** or **FAQ** answers; **2–4 sentence** featured-snippet-style answers when the section genuinely resolves the query.
- **Examples:** how do I calculate my macros, what macros should I eat to lose fat, intermittent fasting macros how to set them, fat loss plateau what to do with macros, PSMF diet what to eat, how much protein per pound when cutting, etc.

### Tier 4 — Informational / Academy growth

- **Role:** Definitions, education, comparisons, lifestyle framing; supports topical authority and **internal linking**.
- **Use:** Explainers, “what is…”, myth vs reality, cross-links to other **`/guides/[slug]`** articles; language for **`tags`**, **`excerpt`**, and supporting paragraphs—not keyword stuffing.

### Operational rules (per article)

- **Pick:** **1 primary** keyword (usually **Tier 2** or **Tier 3** for guides), **3–6 secondary** terms (mix **Tier 3** questions + **Tier 4** support), and **≤2 Tier‑1 touches** unless the piece is **explicitly** calculator- or homepage-focused.
- **Forbidden:** Pasting long tier lists into a single article; **keyword stuffing**; repeating the same Tier‑1 phrase in every section.
- **Required mapping:** Chosen primary → **`metaTitle`**, **`metaDescription`**, first **~100 words** of **`body`** (or hero intro where used), and **at least one H2** that matches the promise; long-tails → **H2/H3** or **FAQ** **only** when that section **answers** the query.
- **Internal links:** Tier‑2 intent should tie to real **`/macros/...`** and **`/guides/...`** paths; **confirm slugs** in the repo before merge.
- **Tone / safety:** Unchanged—**general fitness education**; medical disclaimers and extra care for aggressive protocols (e.g. PSMF).

### Source of truth (optional)

- If the team maintains a **canonical keyword spreadsheet** or strategy doc, add one line in the article briefing: **Source of truth:** `[link or repo path]` — this rule **summarizes usage**; the spreadsheet may add/remove terms by quarter.

